--- Numbers are held as the IR types them, in both modes: a list the
--- program grows as a list is a list, a tensor is a tensor, and where one
--- is assigned to a variable that holds the other it is converted where
--- they meet. Compiled, `xs = [1.5]` into a list did not build (a tensor is
--- not a `Vec`); the interpreter held a tensor where the IR said a list, and
--- a collecting loop of ints was a tensor of floats, which only its values'
--- own choice of row had read.
use math
xs = []
if len[xs] eq 0
    xs = [1.5]
xs = push[xs, 2.5]
log[len[xs]]
log[xs]
t = [1.0, 2.0]
if len[t] gt 0
    t = range[3]
log[t]
log[sum[t]]
out = for i in range[4]
    i * 3
log[len[out]]
out = push[out, 12]
log[out]
log[out[1] + 1]
